<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     §01  THE MEMORY WALL
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section id="s-memory" data-code="memory">
<div class="section-no">01 — The Memory Wall</div>
<h2>Why Quantization Exists: Fitting the Model</h2>
<p>A single parameter in a neural network is typically stored as a 32-bit float — 4 bytes. Llama-3.1-70B has 70.6 billion parameters. That's <strong>282 GB of raw weight storage</strong> — more than three NVIDIA H100 80 GB GPUs can hold, before even counting activations, KV-cache, or optimizer states.</p>
<p>Quantization replaces each 32-bit float with a lower-precision representation. Cut from 32 bits to 16 bits and the model fits on 2 H100s. Go to 8 bits and it fits on one. Go to 4 bits and a single A100 40 GB can run it. The same model, 8× smaller — with surprisingly small quality loss when done right.</p>
<p>The chart below shows exact numbers for Llama-3.1-70B. Each bar is the total weight storage; the label on the right is how many H100 80 GB GPUs are needed (weights only, excluding activations).</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">llama-3.1-70b — weight storage by precision</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">scroll into view to animate</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body" id="s-memory-bars">
    <div class="results-bars">
      <div class="bar-row">
        <div class="bar-label">FP32</div>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" id="bf-fp32" style="background:rgba(139,92,246,.55)" data-w="100"><span>282 GB</span></div></div>
        <div class="bar-sub" style="color:var(--muted)">4× H100 80 GB</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bar-row">
        <div class="bar-label">BF16 / FP16</div>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" id="bf-bf16" style="background:rgba(139,92,246,.65)" data-w="50"><span>141 GB</span></div></div>
        <div class="bar-sub" style="color:var(--muted)">2× H100 80 GB</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bar-row">
        <div class="bar-label">FP8 / INT8</div>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" id="bf-fp8" style="background:rgba(6,182,212,.6)" data-w="25"><span>70.6 GB</span></div></div>
        <div class="bar-sub" style="color:var(--cyan)">1× H100 80 GB</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bar-row">
        <div class="bar-label">INT4 / FP4</div>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" id="bf-int4" style="background:rgba(16,185,129,.6)" data-w="12.5"><span>35.3 GB</span></div></div>
        <div class="bar-sub" style="color:var(--green)">0.5× H100 80 GB</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bar-row">
        <div class="bar-label">INT2</div>
